      {id:'s2',title:'Validate the offline model and negative cases',html:'<p>Download <a href="labs/m11/network-plan.json" download>network-plan.json</a> and <a href="labs/m11/check_plan.py" download>check_plan.py</a>. Run the checker, remove the AWS return route and exceed backup capacity to demonstrate failure. Restore the worksheet. This inspects a model only.</p>'},
      {id:'s3',title:'Create the two-VPC inventory',html:'<p>Follow the runbook for customer 10.60.0.0/16 and AWS 10.80.0.0/16, separate management and workload subnets, explicit route associations and scoped security groups. Do not add peering or TGW shortcuts.</p>'},
      {id:'s4',title:'Prepare the customer appliance and test hosts',html:'<p>Install strongSwan in the stated swanctl model, record versions, disable the appliance source/destination check, enable forwarding and restrict the test flow. Start the private HTTP target. Preserve management independently of the VPN.</p>'},
      {id:'s5',title:'Create VGW, customer gateway and static VPN',html:'<p>Use the appliance EIP as the customer gateway address. Configure both AWS tunnel options as specified, add the customer route and the AWS subnet return route. Protect downloaded tunnel configuration and pre-shared keys.</p>'},
      {id:'s6',title:'Configure and test tunnel 1',html:'<p>Populate <a href="labs/m11/swanctl.conf.example" download>swanctl.conf.example</a> in a root-only file on the disposable appliance. Activate only tunnel 1, confirm installed IPsec state and record a bounded HTTP response from the customer worker.</p>'},
      {id:'s7',title:'Break and restore only the return route',html:'<p>From the external operator session remove the AWS workload subnet route for the customer prefix. Record the request timeout, restore the exact route and verify the response recovers. Save route snapshots and timestamps.</p>'},
      {id:'s8',title:'Observe outage and manual tunnel recovery',html:'<p>Terminate tunnel 1 and observe the bounded request failure. Initiate tunnel 2 and verify the same request succeeds. This intentionally demonstrates manual recovery, not automatic HA. Restore the documented baseline afterward.</p>'},
      {id:'s9',title:'Explain evidence and DNS boundaries',html:'<p>Complete the evidence table in the runbook. Distinguish configuration, tunnel state, observed HTTP and missing evidence. Draw inbound/outbound DNS flows offline; the base lab does not deploy Resolver endpoints or DX.</p>'},
      {id:'s10',title:'Delete and verify recorded resources',html:'<p>Delete the VPN connection, lab instances and storage, release the EIP and remove the recorded gateway/network resources in dependency order. Verify asynchronous deletions and check delayed billing. Retain only redacted evidence.</p>'}
